# LTspice Temperature Effect on 1N4148 Diode

## Objective
The same 1N4148 diode was simulated at *25 °C* and *75 °C* using LTspice.

## Circuit
A DC sweep test circuit was used:

V1 -> 1k resistor -> 1N4148 diode -> ground

Sweep range:
-5 V to 1 V

## Results
At *25 °C, the diode started conducting at approximately **0.48 V*.

At *75 °C, the turn-on voltage shifted lower to about **0.43 V*.

The reverse leakage current also increased slightly at the higher temperature.

## Explanation
Temperature affects diode behavior because higher temperature increases the number of free charge carriers inside the semiconductor material.

This reduces the forward voltage required for conduction and increases reverse leakage current.

This matters in real electronic systems because temperature changes can affect voltage drop, power losses, leakage current, and reliability. Engineers must consider temperature effects when designing stable circuits.
